# t_ns,cam_index,sha256 of the gray8 360x640 pixels the C++ lane consumed.
#
# RoboCap has no C++-emitted digest file: basalt_vio does not write one. These
# digests were computed on 2026-09-08 from the raw session files on the NAS,
# with the recipe the fork's own file-fed driver uses
# (`repos/basalt/python/drive_files.py:SequentialDecoder`): PyAV, one decoder
# thread, one `reformat(width=w/3, height=h/3, format="gray8",
# interpolation="AREA")` call = the C++'s `sws_scale` with `SWS_AREA`
# (`src/io/dataset_io_robocap.cpp:249`), digested over the h x w uint8 buffer.
#
# Source files, in the fed camera order ('left', 'left_front', 'right_front', 'right'):
#   /mnt/nas/datasets/robocap/f408193e6447b3b0_session_15/video_dev4_session15_segment1_left.mp4
#   /mnt/nas/datasets/robocap/f408193e6447b3b0_session_15/video_dev1_session15_segment1_left-front.mp4
#   /mnt/nas/datasets/robocap/f408193e6447b3b0_session_15/video_dev5_session15_segment1_right-front.mp4
#   /mnt/nas/datasets/robocap/f408193e6447b3b0_session_15/video_dev3_session15_segment1_right.mp4
# The first 12 framesets of session 15 (t_ns is the frameset's median plus
# the 14902432 ns camera offset, the clock every basalt CSV carries).
